4. Commercial Use

   (a) You may NOT make Commercial Use of any Covered Work that meets the
       Five Percent Threshold unless you first get Written Permission from
       the Licensor.

   (b) On the conditions in Section 12(b), you MAY make Commercial Use of
       a Derivative Work that does NOT meet the Five Percent Threshold.

   (c) Images, audio, video, and fonts made by the Licensor, whether
       stored as separate files or embedded in other files (for example as
       data URIs), may not be used commercially at all without Written
       Permission, no matter how much else you use.

   (d) "Written Permission" means a document, on paper or electronic,
       that is signed by the Licensor (an electronic signature counts),
       names you, and clearly grants Commercial Use. While the Licensor is
       under 18, Written Permission is valid only if a parent or legal
       guardian of the Licensor also signs it. Nothing else counts as
       permission, including: silence, delay, not enforcing this license,
       accepting a donation or payment, merging your code, replying to a
       message, or any statement that is not signed. Written Permission
       covers only what it says, only for the party it names, and cannot
       be transferred unless it says so.

5. Credit (Attribution)

   Every Covered Work you share, publish, or run for others must:
     (a) keep this license file and the copyright notice above, unchanged,
