10. Ending This License

   (a) If you break any term of this license, all of your permissions end
       automatically. You must then stop using and sharing every Covered
       Work.
   (b) Cure. If you stop a violation, your permissions come back
       automatically: (1) provisionally, from the day you stop, unless
       the Licensor ends them by notice within 60 days after that day;
       and (2)
       permanently, if you fix the violation within 30 days after first
       getting notice of it from the Licensor and it is the first time you
       have received notice. This does not apply to Commercial Use of a
       Covered Work that meets the Five Percent Threshold without Written
       Permission. For that, permissions come back only by Written
       Permission.
   (c) Ending or getting back permission does not cancel what you owe for
       past violations. The Licensor may use every remedy the law allows,
       including court orders to stop you, damages, and your profits from
       the unauthorized use.

